# MongoDB connection string
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017

# Secret key for signing every session token. Generate your own — the server
# refuses to start on the old placeholder, because a key that ships in the
# repository lets anyone mint a token for any account here:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 48
#
# Left unset, the server generates one per boot and says so; that works, but
# everyone is signed out on every restart.
JWT_SECRET=

# Web Push.
#
# VAPID_SUBJECT is how a push service reaches whoever runs this instance, and
# is worth setting: it defaults to SERVER_URL when that is https, and failing
# that to mailto:admin@localhost, which is not a real address. How strictly
# that is enforced is decided per service, so leaving it unset tends to show up
# as push arriving on one browser and not another rather than as a clear
# failure. Must be a mailto: or https: URL. The server warns at boot when it
# has fallen back.
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:admin@example.com
#
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY is optional: on first boot the server generates a keypair
# and stores it, which is enough for push to work. Set it only to hold the key
# outside the database — it is the base64url raw P-256 scalar.
#
# Changing it, or losing the stored pair, invalidates every subscription
# already enrolled: a browser cannot tell that the key moved, so it keeps a
# subscription the push service will refuse forever. Devices repair themselves
# on their next load (the client compares the two keys and re-enrols), but
# every one of them has to open the app before push reaches it again.
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
